```java
import java.util.*;

public class Solution {
    public String findStringWithMaxFrequency(String[] A, String[] B) {
        Map<String, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        
        // Count the frequency of each string in both arrays
        for (String str : A) {
            if (!map.containsKey(str)) {
                map.put(str, 1);
            } else {
                map.put(str, map.get(str) + 1);
            }
        }
        
        for (String str : B) {
            if (!map.containsKey(str)) {
                map.put(str, 1);
            } else {
                map.put(str, map.get(str) + 1);
            }
        }

        // Find the maximum frequency
        int maxFrequency = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        String result = "";

        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : map.entrySet()) {
            if (entry.getValue() > maxFrequency) {
                maxFrequency = entry.getValue();
                result = entry.getKey();
            }
        }

        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Solution solution = new Solution();

        String[] A = {"abc", "bcd"};
        String[] B = {"xyz", "yza"};

        System.out.println(solution.findStringWithMaxFrequency(A, B)); // Output: abc
    }
}
```

This Java code uses a HashMap to store the frequency of each string in both arrays. Then it finds the maximum frequency and returns the corresponding string. If there are multiple strings with the same maximum frequency, this method will return one of them arbitrarily.

Please note that if you need to find all strings with the maximum frequency, you would have to modify the code like so:

