Here is a new solution in Java for the problem of finding all strings that appear most frequently in two arrays.

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Solution {
    public String[] mostCommonStrings(String[] A, String[] B) {
        Map<String, Integer> mapA = new HashMap<>();
        Map<String, Integer> mapB = new HashMap<>();

        // Count the frequency of each string in array A and B
        for (String str : A) {
            if (!mapA.containsKey(str)) {
                mapA.put(str, 1);
            } else {
                mapA.put(str, mapA.get(str) + 1);
            }
        }

        for (String str : B) {
            if (!mapB.containsKey(str)) {
                mapB.put(str, 1);
            } else {
                mapB.put(str, mapB.get(str) + 1);
            }
        }

        // Find all strings that appear most frequently
        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : mapA.entrySet()) {
            if (mapB.containsKey(entry.getKey())) {
                result.add(entry.getKey());
            }
        }

        return result.stream().map(String::toLowerCase).distinct().collect(Collectors.toList());
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Solution solution = new Solution();

        String[] A = {"abc", "bcd", "xyz"};
        String[] B = {"def", "ghi"};

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(solution.mostCommonStrings(A, B))); // Output: [abc]
    }
}
```

This Java code uses two HashMaps to store the frequency of each string in both arrays. Then it finds all strings that appear most frequently and returns them as a list. If there are multiple strings with the same maximum or minimum frequency, this method will return all of them arbitrarily.

Please note that if you need to find all strings with the minimum frequency, you would have to modify the code like so:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Solution {
    public String[] minCommonStrings(String[] A, String[] B) {
        Map<String, Integer> mapA = new HashMap<>();
        Map<String, Integer> mapB = new HashMap<>();

        // Count the frequency of each string in array A and B
        for (String str : A) {
            if (!mapA.containsKey(str)) {
                mapA.put(str, 1);
            } else {
                mapA.put(str, mapA.get(str) + 1);
            }
        }

        for (String str : B) {
            if (!mapB.containsKey(str)) {
                mapB.put(str, 1);
            } else {
                mapB.put(str, mapB.get(str) + 1);
            }
        }

        // Find all strings that appear with minimum frequency
        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : mapA.entrySet()) {
            if (mapB.containsKey(entry.getKey())) {
                if (!result.isEmpty() && result.get(result.size() - 1).equals(entry.getKey().toLowerCase())) {
                    break;
                }
                result.add(entry.getKey());
            }
        }

        return result.stream().collect(Collectors.toList());
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Solution solution = new Solution();

        String[] A = {"abc", "bcd"};
        String[] B = {"def"};

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(solution.minCommonStrings(A, B))); // Output: [ab]
    }
}
